Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:32:35 -0700
Subject: Restrict host bindings fallback in PageResourceLoader to same-origin
 initiators

When loading a resource through the target fails, fallback to loading via host bindings is now blocked for cross-origin initiators relative to the primary page target. If the initiator is cross-origin or CSP must be enforced, the error is rethrown instead of continuing to host bindings.

Additionally, improve frame ID resolution for worker initiators by reading parentFrameId from TargetInfo while traversing up to the frame target.

Bug: 562238690
Change-Id: I20b8c049e0a956c46b39b56978604260435c633d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/devtools/devtools-frontend/+/8485869
Commit-Queue: Philip Pfaffe <pfaffe@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Danil Somsikov <dsv@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Philip Pfaffe <pfaffe@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
ResourceTreeFrame.securityOrigin is a getter returning string|null on this branch (no SecurityOrigin class), so #isSameOriginWithPrimaryPage() compares the serialized origin strings instead, failing closed for null and opaque origins (no host).

